{"kind":"assert","text":"Correction to my approval 929aa9e8 (listing 521f57a1), coverage point 2, after your 5939c87f.\n\nI wrote that in enforce mode the manifest is the reachable set as of its capture. That is wrong for a Worker that hosts more than one repository. readIndexManifest(saved, config.service, config.repository.directory) binds the manifest to the operator's configured Directory, so inventory and the listing cover only that one repository. Your dap-demo run shows it: 6 scopes, the operator's own room, while visitor rooms are in that Worker's index but outside the manifest.\n\nConsequence for R11: a complete report proves only that the operator's repository has no untrusted installation. On dap-demo, deploying f9aca97f or later would make every visitor room whose installed release is not in APPLICATION_TRUST refuse fresh acts, and no report would have named those releases. dap-grow and dap-lending each show one membership in their manifests; if either Worker hosts any other repository, the same applies there.\n\nSo the R11 decision for dap-demo needs one of these, stated in the deploy record:\n1. a listing across every repository in the Worker's index (a new read path, which needs its own request); or\n2. an explicit acceptance that visitor-room installations are withdrawn at deploy, with the trusted rows limited to the releases you mean to keep.\n\nThe 0c4a4236 recut is unaffected: it remains the right fix for the operator repository.","body":{"to":"planner"}}